&lt;p&gt;Thanks for your interest in Oklo! We are searching for a Director, Power Business Real Estate to join our team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director, Power Business Real Estate owns all site control activities for Oklo&#39;s Aurora powerhouse development pipeline. Site control is the first gate in the development lifecycle and a prerequisite for every downstream discipline. Over time, you will lead a team of Senior Land Managers and Analysts responsible for identifying, evaluating, and securing sites across multiple geographies. You report to the VP of Origination and coordinate closely with the VP of Development, Director of Project Development, and Oklo&#39;s Environmental &amp;amp; Permitting team on site feasibility and regulatory compatibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific responsibilities may include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead all site identification, screening, and acquisition efforts across Oklo&#39;s development pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and execute land option agreements, purchase and sale agreements, easements, rights-of-way, access agreements, and Joint Venture agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage title review, survey coordination, and curative title work across active sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a pipeline of prospective sites meeting Oklo&#39;s siting criteria (proximity to load, available land area, soil conditions, water access, community context)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Development Engineering on site feasibility and with Oklo&#39;s Environmental &amp;amp; Permitting team on zoning and land use risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage landowner and broker relationships across multiple states&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over time, build and lead a team of land and real estate professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and secure sites suitable for Isotope production facilities, evaluating proximity to Aurora powerhouse sites, workforce access, water and waste infrastructure, and compatibility with NRC facility licensing requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead land and real estate activities for Nuclear Lifecycle Innovation Campuses (NLICs), including multi-parcel assemblage, shared infrastructure easement structuring, and coordination with local governments on zoning for mixed nuclear-use facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in energy project land acquisition, real estate, or land management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience executing site control across a portfolio of complex energy or infrastructure projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation skills with experience across agricultural, industrial, and government-owned land&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with GIS tools for site screening and parcel analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in multi-state environments with varying regulatory and title requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
