&lt;p&gt;Thanks for your interest in Oklo! We are searching for an experience Electrical Engineer to join our engineering team and support delivery of the Aurora powerhouse at Idaho National Laboratory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Electrical Engineer will serve as a key owner-side technical lead, coordinating electrical design and execution across Oklo teams, EPC partners, equipment vendors, and construction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is focused on delivering complete, coordinated, and constructible electrical systems, not designing in isolation. The successful candidate will take ownership of electrical scope, resolve interfaces and design inputs, review EPC and vendor deliverables, and drive issues to closure in support of procurement, construction, commissioning, and plant operation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate must be comfortable joining an active project where major design and procurement decisions may already be established and developing practical, technically sound solutions within those constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific responsibilities may include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide owner-side technical leadership for Aurora-INL electrical systems, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own electrical scope from design development through procurement, construction, testing, commissioning, and turnover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate electrical work performed by EPC partners and equipment vendors, ensuring responsibilities and interfaces are clearly defined.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish, review, and maintain electrical design criteria, requirements, calculations, specifications, drawings, and equipment data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review electrical studies, including load flow, short-circuit, protective-device coordination, arc-flash, grounding, and other applicable analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify that electrical requirements and design inputs are consistently incorporated across drawings, specifications, studies, vendor packages, and construction documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead resolution of technical questions, RFIs, design changes, nonconformances, and field issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support equipment procurement by developing technical requirements, reviewing vendor proposals and submittals, and resolving vendor interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with project management and scheduling teams to identify priorities, dependencies, risks, and decisions affecting delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work effectively in a progressive design-build environment where engineering, procurement, and construction activities overlap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support constructability reviews, installation planning, inspections, testing, commissioning, and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote practical, solutions-oriented collaboration while maintaining safety, quality, and technical rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering from an accredited program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eight or more years of progressively responsible electrical engineering experience, including significant experience with power-generation electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with facility power distribution, emergency power, grounding, electrical equipment, and electrical studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing engineering drawings, specifications, calculations, and vendor submittals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of applicable electrical codes and standards, including IEEE standards and relevant building and fire codes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to coordinate work across multiple engineering disciplines, contractors, and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership, organization, communication, and technical problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and close issues in a fast-paced project environment with evolving design information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to succeed in a startup-like environment by working through process gaps, ambiguity, and evolving information without allowing administrative obstacles to stall progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop practical near-term solutions that protect the construction schedule while simultaneously improving processes for future execution, without compromising safety, quality, or technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel to project offices, vendor facilities, and the Aurora-INL construction site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineer license or ability to obtain one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with nuclear or DOE-regulated facilities, including exposure to the additional electrical requirements associated with regulated nuclear facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ten or more years of progressively responsible electrical engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting EPC, progressive design-build execution, and field construction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using ETAP for electrical system analysis, protective-device coordination, and arc-flash studies; CDEGS for grounding studies; and Bluebeam for design and construction document reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with switchyard design and high-voltage utility coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with commissioning, startup, or turnover of industrial electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Electrical Engineer that is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about clean energy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about making advanced fission a reality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing and able to learn quickly&lt;/li&gt;
