&lt;p data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Thanks for your interest in Oklo!&amp;nbsp; We are searching for a Senior Process Controls Engineer for our recycling engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;heading&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Position Description:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The person in this role will be responsible for designing, implementing, troubleshooting, scaling, and monitoring various process control systems for the Oklo fuel recycling facility. Some subsystems may include off-gas separation, and waste immobilization. It will include collaboration with cross-functional teams including those with a focus on facility design, unit process equipment design, and licensing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position could alternatively be fulfilled by someone with experience and/or education in instrumentation and controls, electrical, chemical, or process engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;heading&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Specific responsibilities may include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop systems that meet facility and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and document overall control philosophy – define key control variables, setpoints, and rationale to ensure safe, reliable, and efficient process operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review control system documentation – including instrument loop drawings, logic drawings, cause-and-effect matrices, and interlock schemes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and manage control and alarm strategies – establish alarm priorities, setpoints, and functional descriptions to support operator awareness and system safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and specify control system architecture – covering hardware, software, and network requirements for distributed control systems (DCS), programmable logic controllers (PLCs), and human-machine interface (HMI) applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate technical documentation to be included in regulatory filings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;heading&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Process Controls Engineer that is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated by building, and getting technology deployed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Energized by tackling and overcoming challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about clean energy, and&amp;nbsp;making advanced fission a reality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing and able to learn quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to think differently and do things in new ways&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in a fast-paced, highly-iterative startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited to think creatively, critically, and reflectively about the problems they are solving while not leaning only on what has been done before&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to propose novel and creative solutions to technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to communicate technical content and results verbally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An excellent writer who can write in a modern active voice, so make your cover letter compelling and write it well!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
